# Names that land in a namespace C or C++ reserves. `__bar` and `_Foo` are reserved for any use in
# both; `foo__bar` is reserved in C++ only, which treats a double underscore anywhere as reserved.
# All three are legal DSDL, so the compiler rejects them for those targets and offers an encoding.
uint8 _Foo
uint8 __bar
uint8 foo__bar
uint8 plain
@sealed
